From aebebda560f93bd82b2af863eaae62399bbe3760 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 22:35:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [DOSKUTSU] patch 0321 -- sample the margins the frame dump
 cannot save

Patch 0320 added a clip rect so the thrash direct-to-window tile loop
cannot over-blit past the logical box into the margins that
_dos_center_clear_margins painted black. That clip shipped untested.

It could not be tested. The dump writes the 320x240 box at (ox,oy), so
anything outside the box is invisible to it by construction -- and
outside the box is exactly where an over-blit puts its damage. The other
witness, glass capture, had no lock on the game's video mode for the
cells that would have answered it.

So the dump now counts non-zero pixels in the four rects the centring
code clears and never draws into again, and logs them. Zero means
nothing wrote past the logical box.

It reports counts rather than a verdict. Which path did the writing is
not answerable from here, and a bare PASS would invite the reading that
a clean margin proves the 0320 clip specifically -- when all it proves
is that on this run, in these scenes, nothing landed there. A number
that a reader has to interpret is better than a verdict that interprets
itself wrongly.

Costs nothing unless a dump is due -- it runs inside the per-tick body,
which is already gated on DOSKUTSU_SHOT_TICKS naming that tick.

Emits only when centring is active. On a 320x240 surface there are no
margins to sample and the rects would be degenerate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/graphics/Renderer.cpp | 42 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 42 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp b/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
index aa40ceef..1996c6c4 100644
--- a/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
@@ -5228,6 +5228,48 @@ void Renderer::_shot_dump_if_due()
 
   // Byte count is in the log so a truncated dump is visible without opening
   // the file -- the operator reads logs, not PPMs.
+  // DOS-PORT (patch 0321): sample the margins the dump cannot save.
+  //
+  // The dump writes the logical 320x240 box at (ox,oy), so anything OUTSIDE
+  // the box is invisible to it by construction -- which is exactly where a
+  // draw path that over-blits would put its damage, and exactly why patch
+  // 0320's clip rect could not be verified from surfaces. Round Q had to
+  // leave that as "untested" because the glass capture was unavailable.
+  //
+  // These four rects are the ones _dos_center_clear_margins paints black
+  // and never draws into again. A non-zero count means something wrote past
+  // the logical box -- report the counts rather than a verdict, because
+  // "which path" is not answerable from here and a bare PASS/FAIL would
+  // invite the reading that a clean margin proves the clip specifically.
+  //
+  // Costs nothing unless a dump is due: this runs inside the per-tick body.
+  if (_dos_center_active)
+  {
+    const int mw = win->w, mh = win->h;
+    struct { const char *n; int x, y, w, h; } mr[4] = {
+      {"top",    0,        0,        mw,              oy},
+      {"bottom", 0,        oy + 240, mw,              mh - oy - 240},
+      {"left",   0,        oy,       ox,              240},
+      {"right",  ox + 320, oy,       mw - ox - 320,   240},
+    };
+    unsigned long cnt[4] = {0, 0, 0, 0}, tot = 0;
+    for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++)
+    {
+      if (mr[i].w <= 0 || mr[i].h <= 0) continue;
+      for (int yy = mr[i].y; yy < mr[i].y + mr[i].h; yy++)
+      {
+        const Uint8 *row = base + (size_t)yy * (size_t)win->pitch;
+        for (int xx = mr[i].x; xx < mr[i].x + mr[i].w; xx++)
+          if (row[xx]) cnt[i]++;
+      }
+      tot += cnt[i];
+    }
+    LOG_INFO("[shot-dump] margins tick={} top={} bottom={} left={} right={} "
+             "total={} (non-zero px outside the logical box; 0 = nothing "
+             "drew past it)",
+             t, cnt[0], cnt[1], cnt[2], cnt[3], tot);
+  }
+
   if (ok)
   {
     LOG_INFO("[shot-dump] want={} got={} skew={} WROTE {} bytes={} "
-- 
